Objective:

The objective of this project is to develop a Contact Management System

in C++ using structures, without classes.

Contact details such as ID, name, phone, email and allotted slot number

are stored in a circular doubly linked list,

which allows easy insertion, deletion, searching

and traversal in both forward and backward directions.

Contact slots are managed using an array

so a free slot can be allotted to each new contact.

Deleted contacts are stored in a queue,

which keeps the delete history

and lets the oldest deleted contact be restored.

The project applies circular linked list, array and queue concepts

to solve a real-world contact management problem efficiently.

It follows your Hospital objective line by line and matches your latest code:

Patient became contact, bed became slot, and discharge became delete.
“Re-admitted” became “restored”.
The details list is ID, name, phone, email and slot number, since your code stores email instead of age and disease.
